<title>USA: Green Mountain Coffee Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>Green Mountain Coffee Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WATERBURY, Vt. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>		     Twelve Weeks Ended  Twenty-eight Weeks Ended</p>
<p>			     4/12/97   4/13/96     4/12/97  4/13/96</p>
<p> Net sales		   10,063     8,119	24,475  20,263</p>
<p> Net income		     579	  98	 1,301     777</p>
<p> Net income per share	0.17	0.03	  0.38    0.23</p>
<p>Weighted avg. shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	 3,447,999 3,428,588   3,445,838 3,427,554</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said the increase in net income for both periods of 1997 was due to a reduction in deferred tax asset valuation allowance of $562,000 based on continuing profitable quarterly operating results and long-term projections.</p>
<p>The company said current results include a loss on abandonment of equipment of $218,000 related to expansion.</p>
<p>Full company name is Green Mountain Coffee Inc.</p>
</text>
